  data: {
    LLM: "Turn: Must draw 1st card, then either meld OR draw 2nd card. If drew 2nd, must either meld OR draw 3rd card. If drew 3rd card, cannot meld this turn. No discard pile - only draw and meld. Melds: sequences (3+ same suit, Ace high or low not both) or groups (3+ same rank, different suits). Jokers wild. Key feature: Can rearrange ALL table melds when melding, breaking up existing sets and reforming them, provided you add at least one new card from hand and all table cards end in valid melds. Joker value fixed when played, can be moved if released by substituting actual card it represents. Released joker must be used immediately in new meld, cannot return to hand. Knock: After melding with â‰¤5 points in hand, can knock to end round. No layoffs. Winner has lowest hand. Scoring: Winner scores differences from other players' hands. If winner is not knocker, gets 10-point undercut bonus. Going out completely: 25 bonus. Game to 150: winner gets 100 bonus, all get 25 per hand won.",
    Player: "Turn: Must draw 1st card, then either meld OR draw 2nd card. If drew 2nd, must either meld OR draw 3rd card. If drew 3rd card, cannot meld this turn. No discard pile - only draw and meld. Melds: sequences (3+ same suit, Ace high or low not both) or groups (3+ same rank, different suits). Jokers wild. Key feature: Can rearrange ALL table melds when melding, breaking up existing sets and reforming them, provided you add at least one new card from hand and all table cards end in valid melds. Joker value fixed when played, can be moved if released by substituting actual card it represents. Released joker must be used immediately in new meld, cannot return to hand. Knock: After melding with â‰¤5 points in hand, can knock to end round. No layoffs. Winner has lowest hand. Scoring: Winner scores differences from other players' hands. If winner is not knocker, gets 10-point undercut bonus. Going out completely: 25 bonus. Game to 150: winner gets 100 bonus, all get 25 per hand won.",
    objective: 'Get rid of cards by melding. Knock when hand totals â‰¤5 points to end round. Lowest hand wins round. First to 150+ points ends game and scores bonuses.',
    gameplay: "Turn: Must draw 1st card, then either meld OR draw 2nd card. If drew 2nd, must either meld OR draw 3rd card. If drew 3rd card, cannot meld this turn. No discard pile - only draw and meld. Melds: sequences (3+ same suit, Ace high or low not both) or groups (3+ same rank, different suits). Jokers wild. Key feature: Can rearrange ALL table melds when melding, breaking up existing sets and reforming them, provided you add at least one new card from hand and all table cards end in valid melds. Joker value fixed when played, can be moved if released by substituting actual card it represents. Released joker must be used immediately in new meld, cannot return to hand. Knock: After melding with â‰¤5 points in hand, can knock to end round. No layoffs. Winner has lowest hand. Scoring: Winner scores differences from other players' hands. If winner is not knocker, gets 10-point undercut bonus. Going out completely: 25 bonus. Game to 150: winner gets 100 bonus, all get 25 per hand won.",
